         Town Clerk's Office The Town Clerk's Office is charged with ensuring accurate compliance with constantly changing State Laws relative to the Town Clerk and Registrars of Voters and providing service to the general public, including running the elections (Town, state, and federal), which includes registering people to vote and mailing out absentee ballots.  The Clerk’s Office also keeps vital records (i.e. births, deaths, and marriages, Town Meeting votes, cemetery deeds, and zoning decisions).  The Office also licenses dogs and issues Raffle permits, Tag Sale permits, and Business Certificates.  The links below will help you learn more about our services. Records: Birth Certificates Death Certificates Marriage Certificates Election Results Public Record Requests Town Meeting Records 2026  Street List: Books are available in the office for $20 each (cash/check only). A PDF version of the street listing is available for free upon request. Licenses/Permits: Business Certificates Burial Permits Dog Licenses Marriage Licenses Raffles & Bazaars Tag Sale Licenses Fee Schedule (PDF) Other Helpful Links: View Town Bylaws View Precinct Map 
     

 
